# Citation File Format 1.2.0. See https://citation-file-format.github.io
#
# No email address appears in this file on purpose, so the author field omits
# the optional "email" key. Contact for this project is the issue tracker at
# https://github.com/manunicholasjacob/bibauthor/issues
#
# There is no "doi" key yet. Add one under "identifiers" after the first
# Zenodo deposit, which is what mints the DOI:
#
#   identifiers:
#     - type: doi
#       value: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX
#       description: Archived release on Zenodo

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata.
type: software
title: bibauthor
abstract: >-
  A command line tool and Python library that verifies the AUTHOR LIST of
  every bibliography entry against authoritative metadata from CrossRef,
  arXiv, OpenAlex and Semantic Scholar. Citation checkers usually match on
  title and DOI, which lets a chimeric reference through: a real title, a real
  venue, a real year, and an invented author list. bibauthor grades the author
  list instead, reports a graded verdict per entry, and returns a distinct
  exit code for a mismatch, for an entry it could not check, and for a usage
  error, so it can gate a paper repository's CI without crying wolf.
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-01"
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/manunicholasjacob/bibauthor
url: https://github.com/manunicholasjacob/bibauthor
authors:
  - given-names: Manu Nicholas
    family-names: Jacob
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0007-6589-6572
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
keywords:
  - bibliography
  - bibtex
  - citations
  - author verification
  - hallucination
  - crossref
  - openalex
  - arxiv
  - reproducibility
  - latex
